  "id": "COMPOUND:27096 - PROTEIN:812",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Thelephantin G and 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, mediated through the Kappa-type opioid receptor. This is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Thelephantin G targets the Kappa-type opioid receptor, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including Ginkgolide A and 3-Methylfentanyl. These compounds are known to interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, suggesting a possible pathway where Thelephantin G may exert its effects through a similar mechanism. The high scores across the three paths indicate a consistent and reliable relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Thelephantin G and the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the specific molecular interactions involved.",
